    "created_at": "2015-08-28T18:16:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-08-28T18:16:00Z",
    "body": "Edge is basically reverse-engineering whatever Chrome does, bugs and all.  Can't say I blame them...\n\nThat said, the fact that Chrome mishandles the way `undefined` works when passed for an optional argument is a longstanding problem in Chrome's bindings.  We changed it to the current setup in IDL years ago to support the forwarding/proxying use cases... and then Chrome just didn't bother to implement that change.  Doing that in Chrome's bindings would help more than anything else here.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
